f items in it?\n\n Vasya cannot use the information that was received while looking on inventory in some mode for selection of next actions. I. e. Vasya chooses some set of modes first, and then sees all the results and determines the size. \n\nKnowing the number of a i , x and assuming that Vasya is very smart, check whether he can uniquely determine the number of items in his inventory, and how many modes he will need to do that if he knows numbers a i , x and he is able to know number b i after viewing items in mode i .\n\n## Input\n\nThe first line contains two integers n and x ( 0ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë n ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 5 ,ΓÇë2ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë x ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 9 ). The second line contains integers a i ( 1ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë a i ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 9 ). Some numbers among all a i may be equal.\n\n## Output\n\nOutput the fewest amount of modes required to uniquely determine amount of items in the inventory. If there is no solution output ΓÇë-ΓÇë1 .\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n2 4\n2 3\n```\n```\n2\n```\n\n## Note\n\nIn the second example Vasya is not able to determine items count uniquely because 3 items, as well as 4 items, can be displayed on two pages.","type":"text"}],"contestId":73,"index":"E","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Morrowindows","problemKey":"73-E","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"2 seconds","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/73/problem/E"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 4","number":4,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 5","number":5,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 6","number":6,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 7","number":7,"